1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,925
Lesson 10.2.

2
00:00:02,305 --> 00:00:04,456
Attention-free and linear attention.

3
00:00:05,583 --> 00:00:09,932
Attention compares each token with
all previous ones: a cost that grows

4
00:00:09,932 --> 00:00:13,730
with the square of the context
and a cache that keeps growing.

5
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:18,045
For hardware with fixed, sparse
connectivity, that is a problem.

6
00:00:18,425 --> 00:00:22,550
Today we see alternatives that
mix information across positions

7
00:00:22,550 --> 00:00:26,675
without query-key products: the
attention-free transformer, its

8
00:00:26,675 --> 00:00:29,883
local variants and gated
convolutional attention.

9
00:00:31,017 --> 00:00:35,633
The attention-free transformer,
AFT, proposed by Zhai and colleagues

10
00:00:35,633 --> 00:00:40,113
in twenty twenty-one, computes
each position's output as a sigmoid

11
00:00:40,113 --> 00:00:43,983
gate of the query times a
weighted average of the values.

12
00:00:44,363 --> 00:00:48,796
The weights are exponentials of the
keys plus a learned position bias.

13
00:00:49,176 --> 00:00:52,180
Everything is elementwise
in the model dimension:

14
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:55,001
there is no dot product
between query and key.

15
00:00:56,117 --> 00:01:00,431
Without position biases, the causal
AFT-simple variant has a recurrent

16
00:01:00,431 --> 00:01:04,684
form: it suffices to accumulate two
sums, that of the exponentials of

17
00:01:04,684 --> 00:01:08,197
the keys and that of those
exponentials times the values.

18
00:01:08,577 --> 00:01:11,926
Each new token updates the
sums and reads the output.

19
00:01:12,306 --> 00:01:15,137
We verify with sixty-four
positions that the

20
00:01:15,137 --> 00:01:18,098
parallel and recurrent
forms coincide exactly.

21
00:01:18,478 --> 00:01:23,349
The state is just two vectors, instead
of a cache that grows with the context.

22
00:01:24,450 --> 00:01:26,602
In cost, the difference is large.

23
00:01:26,982 --> 00:01:29,262
For a context of four thousand ninety-six

24
00:01:29,262 --> 00:01:31,821
tokens and dimension
four thousand ninety-six,

25
00:01:32,201 --> 00:01:36,805
the attention scores of a layer
cost about two hundred seventy-five

26
00:01:36,805 --> 00:01:40,996
billion operations, and AFT-simple
about one hundred million.

27
00:01:41,376 --> 00:01:43,483
It is a mixing that is
linear in the context.

28
00:01:43,863 --> 00:01:47,310
The price is expressivity,
because AFT-simple cannot

29
00:01:47,310 --> 00:01:50,690
focus on a specific position
the way attention can.

30
00:01:51,817 --> 00:01:55,898
AFT-conv recovers some
expressivity with local position

31
00:01:55,898 --> 00:01:59,757
biases, learned within a
window, like a convolution.

32
00:02:00,137 --> 00:02:03,669
Gated convolutional attention
follows the same idea: it

33
00:02:03,669 --> 00:02:07,265
mixes each position with its
neighbors through a learned

34
00:02:07,265 --> 00:02:10,541
filter and modulates it
with a multiplicative gate.

35
00:02:10,921 --> 00:02:13,725
The connections are
local and fixed, exactly

36
00:02:13,725 --> 00:02:16,275
what a fixed-degree graph can implement.

37
00:02:17,383 --> 00:02:21,063
For thermodynamic hardware,
these variants have three

38
00:02:21,063 --> 00:02:25,229
virtues: they do not need dense
query-key products, they use

39
00:02:25,229 --> 00:02:29,186
elementwise operations such
as exponentials and sigmoids,

40
00:02:29,566 --> 00:02:33,724
close to a pbit's response, and their
connectivity is local and fixed.

41
00:02:34,104 --> 00:02:37,389
That is why they appear in
language-model designs for

42
00:02:37,389 --> 00:02:41,728
probabilistic chips, like the sparse
transformers of the next lessons.

43
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:46,673
These models serve long contexts
and streaming generation with

44
00:02:46,673 --> 00:02:50,372
constant state, and belong to
the family of efficient mixers

45
00:02:50,372 --> 00:02:53,701
together with linear attention
and state-space models.

46
00:02:54,081 --> 00:02:58,565
In lab twenty-eight you will
train a small AFT-conv model.

47
00:02:59,683 --> 00:03:02,762
Common mistakes: assuming full AFT is

48
00:03:02,762 --> 00:03:06,422
linear, when its full
biases cost quadratic.

49
00:03:06,802 --> 00:03:09,805
Forgetting the numerical
stability of the exponentials.

50
00:03:10,185 --> 00:03:14,373
Expecting attention's recall
capacity from purely local mixing.

51
00:03:14,753 --> 00:03:17,569
And comparing quality with
different parameter counts.

52
00:03:18,683 --> 00:03:23,247
In summary: AFT replaces
attention with a weighted average

53
00:03:23,247 --> 00:03:27,417
with exponential weights
and a gate, all elementwise.

54
00:03:27,797 --> 00:03:32,436
Its simple causal version is recurrent,
with constant state and no cache.

55
00:03:32,816 --> 00:03:36,706
Local variants recover expressivity
with fixed connectivity,

56
00:03:36,706 --> 00:03:40,077
which makes them natural
for thermodynamic hardware.

57
00:03:41,183 --> 00:03:44,400
To practice: write the AFT output.

58
00:03:44,780 --> 00:03:46,573
Derive its recurrent form.

59
00:03:46,953 --> 00:03:50,023
Compare the decode state
size with attention.

60
00:03:50,403 --> 00:03:53,711
And say what attention can
do that AFT-simple cannot.
